# SmartBrain_3000 — environment template.
#
# Copy to "compose/.env" (the only env file Docker Compose loads) if you need to override
# a default below. NEVER commit your real .env — it is git-ignored. Most installs need none.
#
# IMPORTANT: provider API keys (OpenAI/Anthropic/Google) are NOT set here. You enter
# them in the app (Settings -> Cloud providers); they are encrypted at rest and never
# read from the environment. Local models (Ollama/MLX) are configured in the app too.

# Port the app serves on (host + in-container). Default 33000.
# SMARTBRAIN_PORT=33000

# Gmail OAuth redirect helper port — LAN/HTTPS mode ONLY. Google's loopback OAuth redirect is
# http://, which the HTTPS app can't serve, so a loopback-only helper on this port forwards the
# callback to HTTPS. Must DIFFER from SMARTBRAIN_PORT. Default 33001; only bound when TLS is on.
# SMARTBRAIN_OAUTH_HELPER_PORT=33001

# Embedding model for semantic Knowledge search, routed to Ollama via Bifrost. The exact
# tag matters. Keep it LOCAL — a cloud model (e.g. openai/...) sends your KB content
# off-box on every reindex. The installer pulls the default for you.
# SMARTBRAIN_EMBED_MODEL=ollama/nomic-embed-text:v1.5

# Remote access (phone): nothing to set here. Pair in the app — Settings -> Remote access —
# which uses the preconfigured hosted broker (override with SMARTBRAIN_SIGNALING_URL to
# self-host). The from-source Docker alternatives are configured by the installer, not by hand:
#   python3 installer/install.py certs <name>.local <LAN-IP>   # issues the mkcert TLS cert into data/certs/ (LAN/HTTPS)
#   python3 installer/install.py webrtc up                      # persist self-hosted broker/TURN settings
# `webrtc up` persists the SMARTBRAIN_SIGNALING_* (and TURN/ICE) values into compose/.env so they
# survive a restart. SMARTBRAIN_TLS_* and SMARTBRAIN_ALLOWED_HOSTS come from the LAN overlay
# (docker-compose.lan.yml) or your own compose/.env — set SMARTBRAIN_ALLOWED_HOSTS yourself for LAN.
# See docs/08-remote-access.md.
# SMARTBRAIN_SIGNALING_URL must be wss://. The Desktop refuses a plaintext ws:// broker (an
# on-path attacker could swap the answer SDP); only for local development against a broker on
# this machine:
# SMARTBRAIN_ALLOW_INSECURE_SIGNALING=1

# Self-hosted signaling NODE only (compose/docker-compose.signaling.yml reads these from ITS .env,
# not the Desktop's). Defaults shown; every one is optional.
# SIGNALING_STATE_FILE=/state/bindings.json   # desktop_id -> pubkey bindings; unset = in-memory (lost on restart)
# SIGNALING_BINDING_TTL_DAYS=30               # a binding unseen this long may be reclaimed when the map is full
# SIGNALING_ALLOW_LEGACY=0                    # 1 admits unsigned (pre-proof) Desktops for unbound ids — transition only
# SIGNALING_TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1/32,::1/128   # peers allowed to set X-Forwarded-For (compose: 172.16.0.0/12)
# SIGNALING_MAX_CONNS_PER_IP=32               # concurrent sockets per client address
# SIGNALING_IP_HELLO_LIMIT=60                 # hellos per client address...
# SIGNALING_IP_HELLO_WINDOW_SECS=60           # ...per this window
# SIGNALING_OFFER_LIMIT=10                    # offers per phone socket...
# SIGNALING_OFFER_WINDOW_SECS=60              # ...per this window (excess: rate_limited + close)
# SIGNALING_ANSWER_LIMIT=60                   # answers per desktop socket...
# SIGNALING_ANSWER_WINDOW_SECS=60             # ...per this window (excess dropped)

# Native Linux only: the app runs as a non-root user (uid 10001) inside the container, so a
# root-owned ./data bind mount can block DB file creation. If the app can't write to data/,
# run once:  sudo chown -R 10001:10001 ./data   (Docker Desktop on macOS/Windows is unaffected).
